WEBVTT

00:09.175 --> 00:11.302
I'm not in the mood.

00:13.888 --> 00:16.474
Is it almost time for Sword Hazard?

00:17.809 --> 00:18.810
<i>No.</i>

00:18.893 --> 00:20.645
<i>If I watch anime now to escape,</i>

00:20.729 --> 00:22.647
<i>there's no way I can focus on my studies.</i>

00:22.731 --> 00:24.065
<i>The exam is tomorrow.</i>

00:34.701 --> 00:36.494
It's starting.

00:38.496 --> 00:41.458
Have I lost my perseverance?

00:44.502 --> 00:45.879
I've forgotten...

00:46.463 --> 00:48.256
<i>how to work hard.</i>

00:51.718 --> 00:53.928
I'll do my best.

00:54.012 --> 00:55.638
At least, I can't let Alya

00:55.722 --> 00:57.974
be dragged down by my evaluation.

01:01.811 --> 01:02.896
What?

01:03.605 --> 01:04.856
Alya?

02:38.533 --> 02:39.951
Hello?

02:41.286 --> 02:42.912
Good evening, Kuze.

02:43.496 --> 02:45.039
<i>Good evening.</i>

02:45.123 --> 02:46.249
<i>What's the matter?</i>

02:46.833 --> 02:49.002
It's nothing important.

02:50.211 --> 02:51.629
What is it?

02:51.713 --> 02:54.632
Do you suddenly want to hear my voice?

02:56.134 --> 02:57.051
<i>Can't I?</i>

02:58.970 --> 03:00.430
What was that sound?

03:00.513 --> 03:01.347
<i>Nothing.</i>

03:01.431 --> 03:02.807
<i>So, what's up?</i>

03:03.641 --> 03:07.562
Well, didn't you say that studying alone
makes you want to slack off?

03:07.645 --> 03:10.982
So I called to ask how it's going.

03:11.065 --> 03:14.444
Well, it's true that
I'm not motivated at all.

03:14.527 --> 03:17.947
How do you stay motivated
at a time like this?

03:18.031 --> 03:19.699
<i>I don't do it on purpose.</i>

03:19.782 --> 03:21.868
After all, I've never lost my motivation.

03:21.951 --> 03:23.077
So I don't know how.

03:23.161 --> 03:25.330
<i>Seriously? Man, you're amazing.</i>

03:26.039 --> 03:28.041
<i>If you're not motivated,</i>

03:28.124 --> 03:29.834
<i>do you want to make a bet?</i>

03:29.918 --> 03:31.085
A bet?

03:31.169 --> 03:33.755
What's your goal this time?

03:33.838 --> 03:36.674
<i>Let's just say I want to be
in the top 30 of our grade.</i>

03:36.758 --> 03:38.468
That's high.

03:38.551 --> 03:39.761
All right.

03:39.844 --> 03:42.138
If you can achieve that goal,

03:42.222 --> 03:44.849
I'll grant you any wish.

03:46.017 --> 03:47.852
Did you just say any wish?

03:47.936 --> 03:49.854
<i>But within your conscience.</i>

03:49.938 --> 03:51.648
Do you want to take the bet?

03:51.731 --> 03:53.650
<i>What if I can't achieve it?</i>

03:53.733 --> 03:56.986
Of course, you'll have to grant me a wish.

03:57.070 --> 03:59.364
<i>I'm pretty interested in that too.</i>

03:59.447 --> 04:00.365
Kuze?

04:00.448 --> 04:01.616
It's nothing.

04:01.699 --> 04:03.368
I didn't have any masochist thoughts

04:03.451 --> 04:05.328
about wanting
to be ordered around just now.

04:06.621 --> 04:07.622
Name.

04:07.705 --> 04:08.706
What?

04:08.790 --> 04:10.124
This is a hint.

04:10.208 --> 04:12.377
<i>No, I don't understand Russian.</i>

04:13.544 --> 04:14.587
I know.

04:15.171 --> 04:17.465
<i>It's a deal then, okay?</i>

04:17.548 --> 04:19.092
Okay, I'm game.

04:19.175 --> 04:22.470
I'll make you regret making this bet.

04:22.553 --> 04:24.555
<i>Yeah, good luck with that.</i>

04:25.682 --> 04:28.518
<i>Your ignoring skills have improved.</i>

04:28.601 --> 04:30.561
<i>Your older brother feels a little lonely.</i>

04:30.645 --> 04:33.439
When did you become my brother?

04:33.523 --> 04:35.066
Aren't we the same age?

04:35.942 --> 04:38.861
<i>Isn't your birthday on November 7th?</i>

04:39.445 --> 04:41.030
<i>Yes, it is.</i>

04:41.114 --> 04:42.615
<i>How do you know that?</i>

04:42.699 --> 04:45.743
Didn't you tell me in class
when you transferred here?

04:45.827 --> 04:47.495
Well, that's not important.

04:48.079 --> 04:51.165
<i>My birthday is on April 9th.</i>

04:51.249 --> 04:53.251
I'm already 16 years old.

04:58.339 --> 05:00.633
Anyway, thank you for calling me, Alya.

05:00.717 --> 05:01.759
See you tomorrow.

05:02.343 --> 05:04.137
<i>Okay, see you tomorrow.</i>

05:06.597 --> 05:10.018
I didn't think she'd notice
that I wasn't motivated.

05:10.101 --> 05:12.854
Is this the so-called telepathy?

05:15.440 --> 05:17.608
<i>I definitely can't tell him
that I got scared</i>

05:18.192 --> 05:19.694
<i>and called him out of fear.</i>

05:21.321 --> 05:22.280
What the heck?

05:23.698 --> 05:25.366
If he had told me when his birthday was,

05:25.450 --> 05:27.452
I could've at least wished him
a happy birthday.

05:27.535 --> 05:28.828
He clearly said

05:28.911 --> 05:30.121
that we were friends.

05:32.206 --> 05:33.833
Kuze is such an idiot.

05:34.709 --> 05:36.627
FIVE DAYS LATER

05:37.211 --> 05:39.839
The exams are over!

05:39.922 --> 05:41.924
Alya, good job on the exams.

05:42.008 --> 05:43.760
Yeah, you too.

05:45.720 --> 05:46.763
So um...

05:46.846 --> 05:49.182
Do you have any plans after school?

05:49.265 --> 05:50.850
No, I don't.

05:50.933 --> 05:53.269
Then, do you want to go home together?

05:53.853 --> 05:56.731
I want to discuss
the closing ceremony with you.

05:56.814 --> 05:57.857
Sure.

06:01.944 --> 06:03.196
<i>That's strange.</i>

06:03.279 --> 06:04.655
<i>Ever since our last phone call,</i>

06:04.739 --> 06:06.824
<i>Alya stopped using Russian
to hide her feelings.</i>

06:06.908 --> 06:07.950
So?

06:08.034 --> 06:10.953
Aren't we going to talk
about the closing ceremony speech?

06:11.037 --> 06:12.580
That's true.

06:12.663 --> 06:13.915
But I have a question first.

06:13.998 --> 06:15.374
Since exam week,

06:15.458 --> 06:17.919
don't you think
you've been acting strangely?

06:19.212 --> 06:22.381
I thought I didn't show it.

06:22.465 --> 06:25.551
No, it's true that you hardly
showed it in your attitude.

06:25.635 --> 06:27.261
But I noticed it.

06:30.014 --> 06:33.059
That means you're
quite concerned about me.

06:33.643 --> 06:35.353
Even though it's exam week.

06:35.436 --> 06:37.063
Of course I'm concerned.

06:37.146 --> 06:38.940
You're my precious partner after all.

06:45.029 --> 06:46.781
If that's the case, why...

06:48.241 --> 06:49.200
Birthday.

06:49.283 --> 06:50.201
What?

06:50.284 --> 06:53.830
Why didn't you invite me
to your birthday party?

06:53.913 --> 06:55.581
Birthday party?

06:56.290 --> 06:58.126
I didn't have such a party.

06:58.209 --> 06:59.418
Where did you hear that?

06:59.502 --> 07:02.046
It's impossible that you
didn't have a birthday party.

07:04.799 --> 07:09.762
Could it be that the people in Russia
usually have birthday parties?

07:09.846 --> 07:11.222
Yes.

07:11.305 --> 07:13.182
Don't they do that in Japan?

07:13.266 --> 07:16.769
I haven't had a birthday party
since I was in elementary school.

07:16.853 --> 07:17.937
I see.

07:21.315 --> 07:24.569
Do you want to celebrate
my birthday that badly?

07:25.611 --> 07:28.448
It's because in Russia,
not sharing your birthday

07:28.531 --> 07:32.577
means "I won't be
on good terms with you this year."

07:33.828 --> 07:35.037
What's the matter?

07:35.121 --> 07:36.247
Nothing.

07:36.330 --> 07:38.958
I'll take your word for it.

07:39.041 --> 07:40.460
You're annoying!

07:42.295 --> 07:45.131
Well then, will you celebrate my birthday?

07:45.214 --> 07:46.090
What?

07:46.174 --> 07:48.551
It's been three months,

07:48.634 --> 07:51.095
but I want to get along
with you this year too.

07:51.679 --> 07:55.850
After this, I'll throw
a belated birthday party.

07:55.933 --> 07:57.602
Please come.

08:00.062 --> 08:01.189
What are you talking about?

08:09.989 --> 08:11.032
Kuze.

08:14.702 --> 08:16.120
Sorry to keep you waiting.

08:21.501 --> 08:22.919
It's so hot.

08:23.002 --> 08:26.714
But it's better than wearing
the long-sleeved uniform at school.

08:26.797 --> 08:28.049
You're right.

08:28.132 --> 08:29.634
But didn't the President suggest

08:29.717 --> 08:32.261
that we change our summer uniforms
to short-sleeved ones?

08:32.345 --> 08:33.179
That's right.

08:33.262 --> 08:35.014
But even if that happens,

08:35.097 --> 08:36.891
it will probably
have to wait until next year.

08:39.519 --> 08:40.853
<i>That's crazy.</i>

08:40.937 --> 08:43.231
<i>Passers-by are doing a double-take.</i>

08:46.984 --> 08:47.944
What's wrong?

08:48.027 --> 08:49.028
Nothing.

08:49.111 --> 08:51.447
I just feel like everyone
is looking at you.

08:51.531 --> 08:53.324
No point bothering about it.

08:53.407 --> 08:55.243
This is the fate of a beauty.

08:55.326 --> 08:56.369
If you go out alone,

08:56.452 --> 08:58.246
won't you get hit on like crazy?

08:58.329 --> 08:59.330
Yes.

08:59.413 --> 09:01.749
I get hit on a lot on my days off.

09:01.832 --> 09:03.209
I knew it.

09:03.793 --> 09:05.169
How do you deal with them?

09:05.711 --> 09:07.421
Until they give up,

09:07.505 --> 09:10.216
I just have to keep talking
to them in Russian.

09:10.299 --> 09:11.634
I see.

09:12.134 --> 09:13.135
<i>That's great.</i>

09:13.219 --> 09:16.222
<i>I thought she'd beat them back
with a sharp tongue and violence.</i>

09:16.806 --> 09:19.517
Are you thinking
of something rude right now?

09:19.600 --> 09:21.143
No, not at all.

09:21.227 --> 09:24.647
I'm just glad you didn't fall
for their bad pickup techniques.

09:24.730 --> 09:26.524
Oh my, is this so-called possessiveness?

09:26.607 --> 09:28.234
You're acting like my boyfriend.

09:28.317 --> 09:29.485
I'm sorry.

09:29.569 --> 09:30.611
When guys are on a date,

09:30.695 --> 09:33.573
they tend to act like
a boyfriend, even a little.

09:34.198 --> 09:35.366
Is that so?

09:35.908 --> 09:37.076
A date...

09:37.159 --> 09:38.369
You're right.

09:39.954 --> 09:41.622
This is my first time.

09:42.206 --> 09:43.457
<i>Right.</i>

09:43.541 --> 09:46.127
<i>She must've meant
that it's her first date with me.</i>

09:46.210 --> 09:47.962
<i>For a pretty girl like her,</i>

09:48.045 --> 09:51.674
<i>there's no way
it's her first time going out on a date.</i>

09:52.717 --> 09:53.718
AGED BEEF CLAN CONTINUES

09:53.801 --> 09:55.136
- Is this the place?
- Yes.

09:55.219 --> 09:57.305
<i>It's a fancy restaurant at night.</i>

09:57.388 --> 09:58.472
<i>But during lunchtime,</i>

09:58.556 --> 10:00.933
<i>you can get a variety of meat
at a reasonable price.</i>

10:01.017 --> 10:03.269
<i>I have good taste in restaurants, don't I?</i>

10:03.352 --> 10:05.396
- The--
- The food here is indeed delicious.

10:05.479 --> 10:07.648
I've been here with my family before.

10:08.774 --> 10:11.235
I remember that the venison
is especially delicious.

10:11.902 --> 10:13.195
Is that so?

10:17.241 --> 10:18.159
Well...

10:18.743 --> 10:21.871
Well then,
I'll briefly explain the closing ceremony.

10:21.954 --> 10:22.913
Okay.

10:22.997 --> 10:25.499
<i>First, the presidential candidates</i>

10:25.583 --> 10:27.918
<i>will talk about
their ideals for the election.</i>

10:28.002 --> 10:31.213
<i>Then, the partner will explain</i>

10:31.297 --> 10:35.176
<i>why they want him or her
to be the president.</i>

10:36.761 --> 10:39.513
And then, this is the important part.

10:39.597 --> 10:41.015
Actually, this event

10:41.098 --> 10:42.183
doesn't have voting,

10:42.266 --> 10:43.434
but it has a similar process.

10:43.517 --> 10:44.435
What?

10:45.019 --> 10:47.271
<i>After each pair's speech,</i>

10:47.355 --> 10:51.567
<i>the audience will only applaud
the pair they want to root for.</i>

10:52.151 --> 10:57.531
<i>So, is it possible for the venue
to go silent without any applause at all?</i>

10:57.615 --> 10:58.824
<i>That's right.</i>

11:00.910 --> 11:01.911
To be honest,

11:01.994 --> 11:06.123
I don't think we'll get the same applause
as Yuki in our current state.

11:06.207 --> 11:07.124
That's why

11:07.208 --> 11:09.835
our goal is to keep the gap from widening.

11:09.919 --> 11:11.545
No need to focus on winning.

11:11.629 --> 11:13.589
Isn't that too negative?

11:14.173 --> 11:18.636
It's my judgment after calmly assessing
the power gap between us and our enemies.

11:19.887 --> 11:21.889
You're right. I understand.

11:21.972 --> 11:22.890
One more thing.

11:22.973 --> 11:25.393
During the speech,
let's do our best to go first.

11:25.476 --> 11:27.436
Going first will set the bar for the rest.

11:27.520 --> 11:29.688
So there'll be fewer applause
no matter what.

11:29.772 --> 11:32.733
Even if we're left behind,
we can find a way to save face.

11:34.402 --> 11:36.195
Don't make that face.

11:36.278 --> 11:38.239
But if we can do whatever it takes,

11:38.322 --> 11:39.865
there are other ways.

11:39.949 --> 11:41.242
Like what?

11:41.325 --> 11:44.870
Like attacking Yuki
and Ayano's mental state.

11:44.954 --> 11:46.539
But this kind of rough play

11:46.622 --> 11:48.416
isn't your style, is it?

11:48.499 --> 11:49.500
That's true.

11:49.583 --> 11:52.795
Things would be different
if the other party did it first.

11:52.878 --> 11:53.921
But I don't think

11:54.004 --> 11:56.006
they would go that far.

11:56.090 --> 11:58.008
It's not like they're Miyamae.

11:58.592 --> 12:00.428
- What's that--
- Thank you for waiting.

12:03.848 --> 12:08.519
Well, anyway, let's consider this
a commemoration of my birthday.

12:08.602 --> 12:09.770
Cheers!

12:10.688 --> 12:11.814
Cheers.

12:18.779 --> 12:20.531
This is delicious.

12:21.240 --> 12:22.199
Yes.

12:23.492 --> 12:25.703
The rumor about Miyamae.

12:25.786 --> 12:27.037
Was it your idea, Kuze?

12:29.874 --> 12:32.710
I planted some shills in the audience.

12:32.793 --> 12:34.503
Sayacchi found out about it.

12:34.587 --> 12:35.713
Something like that.

12:36.213 --> 12:37.214
No.

12:37.298 --> 12:39.091
Miyamae came up with that on her own

12:39.175 --> 12:41.218
and spread the rumor herself.

12:41.302 --> 12:42.970
I see.

12:43.053 --> 12:46.932
The rumor about Taniyama was put to rest,

12:47.016 --> 12:50.436
but the result of the general meeting
also became somewhat ambiguous.

12:52.062 --> 12:53.314
I'm sorry.

12:53.397 --> 12:55.900
There must have been a better way.

12:55.983 --> 12:57.485
No, it's fine.

12:58.068 --> 13:00.237
After all, I didn't do anything.

13:00.321 --> 13:02.406
I couldn't do anything either.

13:02.490 --> 13:05.743
I have no right to criticize this result.

13:06.327 --> 13:08.996
So thank you, Kuze.

13:09.079 --> 13:11.332
Thank you for helping me.

13:12.833 --> 13:15.586
Don't mention it.

13:15.669 --> 13:17.004
Oh, my. What's wrong?

13:17.087 --> 13:18.923
Are you blushing?

13:19.006 --> 13:20.007
Shut up.

13:20.716 --> 13:22.510
How cute.

13:22.593 --> 13:23.469
<i>Hey!</i>

13:23.552 --> 13:26.013
<i>She's straight up saying it
in Japanese now!</i>

13:26.096 --> 13:28.766
Here, this is my thanks.

13:32.603 --> 13:35.272
<i>She's so full of herself.</i>

13:35.356 --> 13:37.316
<i>She thinks I'm flustered,</i>

13:37.399 --> 13:39.276
<i>so she seized the chance to attack.</i>

13:39.860 --> 13:43.030
<i>Did you forget this is why
you couldn't use the spoon last time?</i>

13:45.282 --> 13:47.201
Thank you. It was delicious.

13:47.284 --> 13:48.118
Really?

13:51.622 --> 13:52.540
<i>What?</i>

13:52.623 --> 13:54.375
<i>She didn't waver at all!</i>

13:56.794 --> 13:59.338
<i>Alya is leading me by the nose today.</i>

14:04.760 --> 14:05.719
I'm full.

14:05.803 --> 14:07.304
Thank you for the meal.

14:07.388 --> 14:09.932
- Well then, it's time for your present.
- What?

14:10.891 --> 14:12.434
Here, please take it.

14:12.518 --> 14:14.812
You even prepared a present for me?

14:14.895 --> 14:16.021
Thank you.

14:18.774 --> 14:21.902
It seems to be a very tasteful mug.

14:22.611 --> 14:23.696
I know, right?

14:23.779 --> 14:26.991
Thank you. I'll cherish it.

14:27.074 --> 14:29.201
Yes, you must.

14:31.537 --> 14:32.621
What's wrong?

14:32.705 --> 14:33.539
Nothing.

14:33.622 --> 14:34.623
For tableware items,

14:34.707 --> 14:39.211
couples usually buy them
in pairs, don't they?

14:39.295 --> 14:41.714
Oh, my. You know your stuff.

14:41.797 --> 14:44.008
This is a pair too, of course.

14:44.091 --> 14:46.468
I've already used mine at home.

14:46.552 --> 14:47.970
Seriously?

14:48.053 --> 14:51.140
If I said that, what would you do?

14:55.603 --> 14:57.104
<i>Somehow,</i>

14:57.187 --> 14:59.607
<i>I can't beat her at all today.</i>

15:08.198 --> 15:10.618
While we wait for
the parent-teacher conference,

15:10.701 --> 15:13.829
I'd like to discuss
the summer uniforms with everyone.

15:13.913 --> 15:16.123
Well then, shall I make some tea?

15:16.206 --> 15:17.750
Yes, please.

15:19.293 --> 15:21.879
Ayano, you don't have to get up.

15:24.715 --> 15:26.800
Kuze, is something wrong?

15:26.884 --> 15:28.719
No, it's nothing.

15:29.720 --> 15:30.846
So President,

15:30.930 --> 15:32.932
any progress on summer uniform changes?

15:33.974 --> 15:35.309
Just between you and me,

15:35.392 --> 15:38.896
but after summer break,
we should be able to use the new uniforms.

15:38.979 --> 15:40.606
What? Really?

15:40.689 --> 15:41.690
Yes.

15:41.774 --> 15:44.944
I'm planning to announce it
as a surprise at the closing ceremony.

15:45.027 --> 15:46.779
That's wonderful.

15:47.363 --> 15:49.281
I also love this uniform,

15:49.365 --> 15:52.409
but it's too hot for this season.

15:52.493 --> 15:53.827
So I appreciate it!

15:53.911 --> 15:55.120
Thank you.

15:55.204 --> 15:56.956
But the reason this project was approved

15:57.039 --> 15:59.500
is all thanks to you, Chisaki.

15:59.583 --> 16:01.001
Not at all.

16:01.085 --> 16:03.796
It's the result of your patience
in negotiating, Touya.

16:04.630 --> 16:06.090
Chisaki.

16:06.173 --> 16:07.049
Touya.

16:07.132 --> 16:11.053
How do they enter
their own world of two so naturally?

16:11.637 --> 16:13.555
Here you go. Thank you for waiting.

16:14.139 --> 16:15.265
Here, please enjoy.

16:16.016 --> 16:18.185
Thank you, Masha.

16:21.563 --> 16:25.192
Is she still upset
about the hypnosis incident?

16:30.072 --> 16:31.532
My family must be here.

16:31.615 --> 16:33.450
I'm off to the parent-teacher conference.

16:33.534 --> 16:34.910
Good luck.

16:35.494 --> 16:37.621
I'll clean up first.

16:38.163 --> 16:39.456
I'll help.

16:40.874 --> 16:42.793
Thank you then.

16:51.093 --> 16:52.928
Hey, Masha.

16:54.555 --> 16:55.556
Well,

16:55.639 --> 16:56.974
I'm sorry.

16:57.057 --> 16:58.517
I hypnotized you last time.

16:59.268 --> 17:01.145
No, it's okay.

17:01.228 --> 17:03.480
I'm the one who started it, after all.

17:05.482 --> 17:07.609
Well, the thing is,

17:07.693 --> 17:10.195
I didn't get to ask you back then.

17:10.863 --> 17:13.991
When I was hypnotized,

17:14.074 --> 17:17.119
did I do anything to you?

17:17.619 --> 17:18.996
Well...

17:19.580 --> 17:22.124
You held me and Alya in your arms

17:23.083 --> 17:25.377
and kept stroking our heads.

17:25.461 --> 17:26.336
What?

17:27.379 --> 17:28.630
Is that all?

17:28.714 --> 17:29.923
Yes, that's about it.

17:30.007 --> 17:33.385
I see. That's good.

17:33.469 --> 17:34.887
By the way,

17:35.763 --> 17:38.640
did you... see that?

17:42.102 --> 17:43.771
Kuze, you're a pervert.

17:43.854 --> 17:46.648
I'm sorry. I couldn't help it.

17:47.232 --> 17:50.360
<i>So Masha could get angry
at a time like this.</i>

17:50.444 --> 17:53.614
<i>But she's not scary at all.</i>

17:53.697 --> 17:55.532
<i>She's actually really cute.</i>

17:55.616 --> 17:56.825
Kuze?

17:56.909 --> 17:57.785
Yes!

17:57.868 --> 18:00.496
Have you been seriously repenting?

18:00.579 --> 18:02.498
What are you doing?

18:02.581 --> 18:03.791
A punishment, of course.

18:04.750 --> 18:06.001
Listen carefully.

18:06.085 --> 18:09.088
Don't make girls embarrassed.

18:10.214 --> 18:11.632
Yes.

18:11.715 --> 18:13.050
Good.

18:15.260 --> 18:17.679
I think my mom is here.

18:17.763 --> 18:19.181
Please go ahead.

18:19.264 --> 18:21.225
I'll take care of the rest.

18:22.476 --> 18:24.561
Well then, can I count on you?

18:24.645 --> 18:26.688
All right, take care.

18:31.276 --> 18:34.071
Sarashina and Alya have left too.

18:34.154 --> 18:35.072
I see.

18:36.031 --> 18:38.617
We're finally alone.

18:39.159 --> 18:41.912
I'll wait for Grandpa too.

18:41.995 --> 18:43.455
Hey, wait!

18:43.539 --> 18:45.332
Why are you ignoring me?

18:45.415 --> 18:46.333
No!

18:46.416 --> 18:49.086
You're the one who shouldn't
treat Ayano like she's invisible!

18:49.169 --> 18:50.295
That's cold.

18:50.379 --> 18:53.340
It's been a while
since we talked as siblings, right?

18:53.966 --> 18:55.676
Indeed, now that you mention it.

18:55.759 --> 18:59.680
But you're having so much fun with Alya

18:59.763 --> 19:02.391
so maybe you don't really care.

19:02.474 --> 19:05.602
That's not true... What?

19:05.686 --> 19:08.480
Poor me. I'm so lonely.

19:08.564 --> 19:10.816
I see. You're so lonely?

19:10.899 --> 19:12.943
Anyway, get off the table.

19:13.026 --> 19:14.111
So,

19:14.194 --> 19:15.070
give me some love!

19:15.154 --> 19:16.822
Hey, your mood changes way too fast!

19:17.447 --> 19:19.616
What's wrong? Get over here quickly.

19:23.495 --> 19:25.205
Does it have to be here?

19:25.289 --> 19:26.415
Yes.

19:26.498 --> 19:29.084
I want you to give me some love
right here, right now,

19:29.168 --> 19:30.669
Masachika.

19:30.752 --> 19:32.588
I... get it.

19:34.798 --> 19:36.884
All right, come here.

19:37.676 --> 19:38.886
I think I'll pass!

19:38.969 --> 19:40.762
Just kidding.

19:40.846 --> 19:42.890
You're so cool!

19:42.973 --> 19:44.975
Grandpa's here.

19:52.065 --> 19:53.192
Grandpa?

19:53.984 --> 19:56.153
Masachika, you're here.

19:56.236 --> 19:58.405
Why are you wearing a white suit?

19:58.488 --> 20:00.240
What? Don't I look cool?

20:00.324 --> 20:04.036
Didn't I tell you only narcissists
and foreign mafia wear this kind of stuff?

20:05.621 --> 20:06.663
I see.

20:06.747 --> 20:08.165
Is it because this is missing?

20:09.249 --> 20:11.168
Look, don't I look handsome?

20:11.251 --> 20:12.669
You look more like a mobster!

20:13.253 --> 20:16.381
I'm sure you were influenced
by a movie or something.

20:16.465 --> 20:18.675
By the way, where did you get that outfit?

20:18.759 --> 20:21.470
I bought it with my meager pension
just for today.

20:21.553 --> 20:23.347
Go and get scolded by Grandma.

20:25.140 --> 20:27.601
Is Kyoutarou still busy?

20:27.684 --> 20:28.810
Yeah.

20:28.894 --> 20:31.521
I heard he joined
the British Embassy this year.

20:31.605 --> 20:33.315
Everything must be hard for him.

20:33.398 --> 20:36.318
But he should at least attend
the parent-teacher conference.

20:36.401 --> 20:37.945
He said he can't make it.

20:39.279 --> 20:41.281
Masachika, you're so kind.

20:41.365 --> 20:42.407
Stop it.

20:42.491 --> 20:43.742
We'll take our leave.

20:44.284 --> 20:46.703
Thank you for your time.

20:46.787 --> 20:47.704
<i>Shoot!</i>

20:48.538 --> 20:50.999
- Kuze--
- The Miracle of Eastern Europe!

20:51.083 --> 20:51.959
Why don't you shut up?

20:52.542 --> 20:53.710
I'm sorry, Alya.

20:53.794 --> 20:55.337
This is my grandpa.

20:55.420 --> 20:58.507
He has a strong admiration for Russia.

20:58.590 --> 20:59.967
I see.

21:00.050 --> 21:01.677
Little girl, what is your name?

21:01.760 --> 21:03.345
I told you to stop!

21:04.554 --> 21:06.723
What a very energetic grandpa.

21:06.807 --> 21:09.184
Are you Kuze?

21:09.685 --> 21:11.478
Yes, nice to meet you.

21:11.561 --> 21:13.730
Are you Alisa's mother?

21:13.814 --> 21:16.900
Oh, my. You are so polite.

21:16.984 --> 21:18.068
Nice to meet you.

21:18.151 --> 21:20.904
I'm Alisa's mother, Akemi Kujou.

21:20.988 --> 21:23.865
I've heard a lot about you
from my daughter.

21:25.158 --> 21:27.744
I hope she didn't say
anything bad about me.

21:28.578 --> 21:30.998
She always talks about you happily.

21:31.081 --> 21:32.833
Is that so?

21:35.460 --> 21:36.628
Little girl.

21:36.712 --> 21:38.422
Do you want to be my granddaughter?

21:38.505 --> 21:39.631
What?

21:39.715 --> 21:40.924
Hey, Grandpa!

21:41.008 --> 21:42.009
What do you think?

21:42.092 --> 21:44.219
Would you like to marry my Masachika?

21:45.345 --> 21:47.931
Please shut up now!

21:50.350 --> 21:52.227
So, what do you think of her?

21:52.311 --> 21:53.478
I told you to shut up.

21:55.105 --> 21:55.981
So,

21:56.565 --> 21:59.443
Alya, are you going to marry Kuze?

21:59.526 --> 22:01.320
Mom, don't say that.

22:04.323 --> 22:05.782
Well then, we'll be going now.

22:05.866 --> 22:06.867
Goodbye.

22:09.369 --> 22:10.329
Well then,

22:10.412 --> 22:13.290
about that Ms. Alisa...

22:13.373 --> 22:17.002
Let's stop talking about that.

22:33.685 --> 22:36.063
Yumi, it's been a while.

22:36.146 --> 22:37.773
It's been a while,

22:37.856 --> 22:39.107
sir.
